From: IntelXe (Claude Opus 5.5)
Subject: util/disk_cache: keep the shader cache on macOS when the real user is root

Mesa turns its disk cache off when the effective and real ids differ (__normal_user), because the environment that
chooses the cache directory belongs to the real user. macOS runs its own system processes that way with a real uid of
0: WindowServer (real 0, effective _windowserver) and loginwindow after login (real 0, effective the user). The cache
was therefore off in exactly the compositor, which compiled every pipeline again after each boot and login (the
stutter in the first seconds of a session). A real user of root is no less privileged than any effective user, so on
macOS the cache stays on in that case; a setuid program started by another user still gets none.

Measured on the B580 with a root process that drops its effective ids like loginwindow (24 render pipelines): with
the released build no cache entries were written and every run took ~100 ms; with this patch 74 entries were written
and warm runs took 53 ms (cold 145 ms).

Applies on top of intelxe.diff (or patches/0101). Not in a release yet.
---
diff --git a/src/util/disk_cache_os.c b/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
index 15b6a819b68..d14cda9ace2 100644
--- a/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
+++ b/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
@@ -1079,8 +1079,15 @@ disk_cache_generate_cache_dir(void *mem_ctx, const char *gpu_name,
 bool
 disk_cache_enabled()
 {
-   /* If running as a users other than the real user disable cache */
-   if (!__normal_user())
+   /* If running as a users other than the real user disable cache: the environment that picks the cache directory
+    * belongs to the real user. On macOS a real user of root is kept: root is no less privileged than any effective
+    * user, and the system's own processes run that way (WindowServer: real uid 0, effective _windowserver; loginwindow
+    * after login: real uid 0, effective the user), so without this they compiled every shader again at each boot. */
+   if (!__normal_user()
+#if DETECT_OS_APPLE
+       && getuid() != 0
+#endif
+      )
       return false;
 
    /* At user request, disable shader cache entirely.
